# Custom Icons

Prefer an existing Iconify set (usually `tabler:*`) before adding a custom icon. If none matches, register one in `src/icons.ts` inside `registerCustomIconifyIcons()` with `addIcon` from `@iconify/vue`. That function is called once from `src/main.ts`.

## Naming

- App icons: `custom:kebab-name` (e.g. `custom:pin-filled`)
- Brand logos with a fixed palette: `brand-*` (e.g. `brand-wati`)

Use the name as `icon` / `leftIcon` on `Button`, or `<Icon icon="custom:pin-filled" />`.

## Registering

`addIcon` injects `body` into Iconify’s own `<svg>`. Pass **inner markup only** (paths, groups, defs). Do not wrap `body` in `<svg>`. Set `width` and `height` to the source viewBox size (usually 20).

- Use `currentColor` for fill and stroke so the icon follows `Button` / `Icon` color classes.
- Hardcoded fills are only for brand logos that must keep a specific palette.
- Stroke-only paths **must** set `fill="none"`. SVG default fill is black; without this the shape renders as a black silhouette. Do not rely on an outer `<svg fill="none">` to inherit that.
- Filled paths keep `fill="currentColor"` (or the brand color).

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
addIcon("custom:pin-filled", {
  body: `<path ... fill="currentColor"/>
<path ... fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>`,
  width: 20,
  height: 20,
});

// ❌ BAD — wrapping svg; stroke paths inherit black fill
addIcon("custom:pin-filled", {
  body: `<svg fill="none">...</svg>`,
  width: 20,
  height: 20,
});
```

Some older entries in `src/icons.ts` still wrap a full `<svg>`. Do not copy that for new icons.
